{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L105","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":105,"end":105}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":105,"end":105},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a3f5107eb8eea774bbadbfdd067e8f6aebfd042eb527ae839ea4032655925333","meta":{"text":"The evaluation outcome: a stamped record (trust `candidate`) + the per-item detail."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L111","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":111,"end":116}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":111,"end":116},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:dbce492bdf348f3467f8de7cf119c32f96cff632d6e08868632caeca59ce7cfb","meta":{"text":"Run the admissibility evaluator over a candidate's evidence with the gate receipt wired in, and\nstamp the final evidence + applicability verdicts onto a fresh {@link MemoryRecord}. Trust stays\n`candidate` — activation / proposal are separate steps that set `local` / `team`. The record's\n`evidence` items are stamped with their per-item verdict + `checkedAt` + `reason`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L166","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":166,"end":166}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":166,"end":166},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:206ec442093a499e1b6d87a715b4dde799e30d8c3ed1c4d3b99a486e6458aabe","meta":{"text":"The snapshot the promotion orchestrator takes before running the gate (no lock held while running)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L175","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":175,"end":179}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":175,"end":179},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:99e9c8fc715ffb8069a8f94aa4ac2435fcfce02e78affdddb8565001fbbc6b92","meta":{"text":"Verify a post-run snapshot matches the pre-run snapshot (PRD line 277: \"verify that candidate,\npolicy, HEAD, and worktree digest are unchanged\"). A mismatch means the gate ran against state that\nhas since drifted → the receipt MUST NOT be trusted and promotion MUST be aborted."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L191","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":191,"end":191}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":191,"end":191},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:509cdc0792e208daac0ec3324babda37031e815b87f20df0403360e17e2a440f","meta":{"text":"A local activation result: what was written + whether cleanup ran (crash-recovery signal)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L201","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":201,"end":206}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":201,"end":206},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:aa254a0510fc697a062fcc5b7700f7c96c41c95fc714f88f63672e5dfe7776bd","meta":{"text":"Activate a candidate's evaluated record LOCALLY (trust `local`). Idempotent + crash-safe\n(PRD line 348): writes the record to `active` + the receipt to `receipts` (both upserts — no-ops on\na re-run), THEN removes the candidate from `candidates`. A crash between the writes and the remove\nleaves a candidate that the next re-run dedupes (same ids → no-op upserts) + re-cleans."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L237","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":237,"end":237}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":237,"end":237},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a9f7313dd817222839bd461c58ffbde6428f38cfd370d358636f7c28c90cc736","meta":{"text":"Thrown when a team proposal is refused (invalid evidence — PRD line 346)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L248","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":248,"end":248}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":248,"end":248},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ae3720b176dc0e76c53e8719b4f464123c8b3ea5d1b47f5620760a94c3410339","meta":{"text":"A team proposal result: the promoted record id + the accept-decision id (both idempotent)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L257","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":257,"end":263}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":257,"end":263},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:f9798803e993ec6db94faa5cd0bd8342972bd208c106d7fe7d67357cc175b081","meta":{"text":"Propose a record for team trust (PRD line 346). Writes the team record (trust `team`) + an `accept`\ndecision + the receipt to the team store. Refuses when the evaluated evidence is `invalid` (the\nclaim is not admissible — it cannot become team-trusted). Idempotent by content id: re-proposing the\nsame claim reproduces identical `mem:`/`dec:`/`rcpt:` ids, so every write is a no-op upsert and the\nteam ledger converges without a cloud service (PRD exit gate line 350)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L308","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":308,"end":316}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":308,"end":316},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:834fa243114c0f54e6aeb37be17c98cb6790fd16de5a7f0cad0e0569c89898c1","meta":{"text":"Propose an ALREADY-ACTIVATED local record for team trust (PRD line 257: `crib memory propose\n<memory-id>`). Unlike {@link proposeTeam} — which takes a freshly-evaluated {@link\nCandidateEvaluation} — this wraps the activated record's stamped verdicts as the evaluation so the\nadmissibility guard runs against the verdicts the gate stamped at activation time. The receipt\npinned the gate run; the record's `verdicts.evidence` is the admissibility result. Refuses an\ninvalid-evidence record (PRD line 346) and is idempotent by content id (re-proposing reproduces\nidentical `mem:`/`dec:`/`rcpt:` ids → no-op upserts)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L39","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":39,"end":39}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":39,"end":39},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:c31c3e7d68002416586625b3c3be4618d37233cb96e7e5611c44be74132ffc6e","meta":{"text":"View a {@link GateReceipt} as the {@link EvalReceipt} subset the evaluator reads."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/memory/src/promotion.ts@L52","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":52,"end":52}},"file":"packages/memory/src/promotion.ts","span":{"start":52,"end":52},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:63ec20980ab7d4cccbcd593e563c68d7f1a46e872ff8704f0fb626bdc5472295","meta":{"text":"A receipts port over an in-memory map (the just-produced receipt + any prior receipts)."}}
